# Wave Action Authoring

When creating or modifying a deployment Apex script:

- Put the script under `scripts/apex/actions/**/*.apex`.
- Include exactly one single-line `smart-deployment-action` JSON header.
- Declare a stable `id`, `phase` (`before` or `after`), and a non-empty `when.components` or `when.types` selector.
- Keep auxiliary Apex without deployment metadata under `scripts/apex/library/`.
- Do not infer or document the dependency only in prose; the header is the plugin contract.
- Run the repository validation command before handing off the change.

Canonical header:

```apex
// smart-deployment-action: {"id":"seed-account-data","phase":"after","when":{"components":["CustomObject:Account"]},"description":"Create records needed by later automation."}
```

The plugin validates this contract, resolves the action to a wave, hashes the script, and pauses at a durable checkpoint. Agents must not execute the script automatically.
